      "body": "## Motivation\n\nUnder prefill CP, `Compressor.compute_kv_score` all-gathers `kv_score` across the CP group in every DeepSeek-V4 layer. On the aiter path (#41931) `kv_score` is a bf16 GEMM output, but it is widened to fp32 before the gather, so the gather moves twice the bytes it needs. On MI355X (DeepSeek-V4-Pro, TP4 + prefill CP4, 16K-token chunk) these gathers take 32 ms of a 580 ms chunk.\n\n## Modifications\n\nWiden `kv_score` after the CP gather instead of before it, on the aiter path only. The gather only moves rows, so the result is bit-identical. Other paths are unchanged.\n\nRelated: #34624 keeps `kv_score` in bf16 through the compress kernels behind `SGLANG_OPT_KV_SCORE_BF16`.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nBit-identical. With this commit, the token ids, logprobs and top-5 logprobs of 5 fixed greedy prompts (including uneven CP shards) match before and after across repeated server launches, and an operator-level check of the gathered `kv_score` is bitwise equal. The path is covered by `test/registered/amd/test_deepseek_v4_pro_fp4_cp.py`.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nMI355X x4, `lmsysorg/sglang-rocm:v0.5.22-rocm10-mi35x-20261018`, DeepSeek-V4-Pro-0813, `--tp 4 --enable-prefill-cp --cp-strategy interleave --attn-cp-size 4 --chunked-prefill-size 16384`, dummy weights:\n\n| TTFT (median) | before | after |\n|---|---:|---:|\n| 16K tokens | 589.7 ms | 574.9 ms (−2.5%) |\n| 64K tokens | 2414.3 ms | 2347.6 ms (−2.8%) |\n\nPer layer, the `kv_score` gather drops from 604 to 310 µs (c4 core), 303 to 155 µs (c128 core) and 155 to 83 µs (indexer); GPU time per 16K chunk goes from 581.6 to 566.4 ms. ROCm 7.2.4 (`v0.5.22-rocm724-mi35x-20261017`) shows the same gain: 16K 588.9 → 574.1 ms, 64K 2391 → 2331 ms.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n",
